4
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,460
Your medical history shows

5
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:09,690
that you had a tumor near the brainstem.

6
00:00:10,010 --> 00:00:11,000
Sun!

7
00:00:11,020 --> 00:00:12,290
Don't worry.

8
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:14,040
I did what you asked.

9
00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:16,490
But our relationship was wrong
from the beginning.

10
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:18,080
Stop talking,

11
00:00:18,410 --> 00:00:19,500
and listen to me.

12
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:22,120
I do love you,

13
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:24,700
but our relationship was wrong
from the beginning.

14
00:00:25,310 --> 00:00:26,710
No...

15
00:00:26,730 --> 00:00:28,000
That's not true.

16
00:00:28,210 --> 00:00:30,080
What she said

17
00:00:30,440 --> 00:00:32,000
makes me think

18
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:35,080
someone tampered with her memories.

19
00:00:36,890 --> 00:00:38,500
I'm sorry, Sun.

20
00:00:44,710 --> 00:00:48,590
♫Trapped in a love that's a fading image,♫

21
00:00:49,830 --> 00:00:52,310
What should I do to make her stay?

22
00:00:53,310 --> 00:00:55,400
Is it too late

23
00:00:56,010 --> 00:00:57,710
to tell her the truth?

24
00:01:01,310 --> 00:01:02,790
Stop talking,

25
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:04,300
and listen to me.

26
00:01:07,890 --> 00:01:09,390
Let me help you.

27
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:15,620
♫But who are you?♫

28
00:01:16,150 --> 00:01:17,370
♫...Please tell me♫

29
00:01:17,390 --> 00:01:18,600
What now, Sun?

30
00:01:20,910 --> 00:01:22,610
Just tell me your excuse already.

31
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:33,010
I don't care how you remember me.

32
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,300
All I ask is that you...

33
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:37,710
remember my embrace.

34
00:01:39,050 --> 00:01:40,710
I want you to know

35
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:43,400
I never meant to hurt you.

36
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:53,500
I'm sorry

37
00:01:54,150 --> 00:01:57,000
I left you with someone evil like Nadear.

38
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:10,260
[Third Person]

39
00:02:12,480 --> 00:02:21,810
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

40
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:27,490
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

41
00:02:27,510 --> 00:02:31,120
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

42
00:02:31,770 --> 00:02:37,530
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

43
00:02:37,550 --> 00:02:46,980
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

44
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:52,440
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

45
00:02:52,470 --> 00:02:56,750
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

46
00:02:56,770 --> 00:03:05,690
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

47
00:03:06,050 --> 00:03:14,210
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

48
00:03:48,610 --> 00:03:50,040
You're back, Chris?

49
00:03:56,610 --> 00:03:57,400
Nadear...

50
00:03:58,460 --> 00:03:59,890
I'm sorry.

51
00:04:00,510 --> 00:04:01,710
I'm so sorry...

52
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:08,000
It's okay.

53
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:15,010
Just having you back is enough for me.

54
00:04:50,310 --> 00:04:51,310
What the hell happened?

55
00:04:56,660 --> 00:04:58,690
How could Chris leave you?

56
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:00,710
Was she...

57
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:02,440
angry

58
00:05:02,590 --> 00:05:04,400
that you'd left her before?

59
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:09,600
No.

60
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:12,820
I haven't even told her that.

61
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:15,880
Nadear made Chris leave me.

62
00:05:17,170 --> 00:05:18,110
How?

63
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:31,390
What are you going to do?

64
00:05:32,810 --> 00:05:35,720
I have to find out what Nadear did to Chris.

65
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:37,300
How?

66
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:46,680
Didn't you tell me

67
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:49,320
that Mrs. Chicha hired a private detective
to look into her husband's affair

68
00:05:49,710 --> 00:05:51,000
and ended up filing for divorce?

69
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:52,500
Uh-huh.

70
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:55,490
When is she coming back to Thailand?

71
00:05:56,690 --> 00:05:57,910
I want to talk to her.

72
00:05:59,870 --> 00:06:01,290
What about your sickness?

73
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:02,500
What are you going to do about it?

74
00:06:09,310 --> 00:06:10,310
I don't care.

75
00:06:10,990 --> 00:06:12,800
I have to save her.

76
00:06:13,410 --> 00:06:15,720
I won't let Chris stay with Nadear anymore.

77
00:06:50,270 --> 00:06:52,120
I hurt you again.

78
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:57,100
Did Dr. Jeen make you remember everything?

79
00:07:01,870 --> 00:07:03,900
I thought I was a good person

80
00:07:04,610 --> 00:07:05,970
who never hurt anyone.

81
00:07:09,420 --> 00:07:11,010
Even after I broke up with you,

82
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:15,070
I still stayed around to help you.

83
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:22,410
I love Sun,

84
00:07:23,790 --> 00:07:25,700
but I've never dated her,

85
00:07:27,300 --> 00:07:28,800
because I'm waiting for the day

86
00:07:28,810 --> 00:07:30,910
we don't have to lie to your parents
about our relationship anymore.

87
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:37,490
What I never thought I'd do is...

88
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:39,810
become the third person.

89
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:44,110
Or make someone else the third person.

90
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:49,700
But the truth is...

91
00:07:53,110 --> 00:07:54,900
I was doing all of that.

92
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:04,990
But I don't get it.

93
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:09,410
Why didn't you want me to know the truth?

94
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:15,800
I just want us to start over

95
00:08:15,820 --> 00:08:17,910
and leave the pain behind.

96
00:08:23,510 --> 00:08:25,900
But I didn't know Sun would come back.

97
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:35,610
I'm sorry

98
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:41,500
for what happened, both then and now.

99
00:08:44,390 --> 00:08:45,700
I promise

100
00:08:47,050 --> 00:08:48,700
I won't hurt you again.

101
00:08:58,410 --> 00:09:00,710
Then let's make things right.

102
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:05,660
From now on,

103
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:07,800
there will be just the two of us.

104
00:09:11,910 --> 00:09:13,510
I love you, Chris.

105
00:09:15,810 --> 00:09:17,610
Can you sleep with me tonight?

106
00:09:31,260 --> 00:09:33,100
I ended things with Sun

107
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:36,420
because she was the other woman.

108
00:09:38,220 --> 00:09:40,410
But I can't date you either,

109
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:45,590
because I don't love you...

110
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:58,300
When I said I wouldn't hurt you again,

111
00:09:58,760 --> 00:09:59,600
I meant...

112
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:04,900
I don't want you to get your hopes up.

113
00:10:08,510 --> 00:10:10,700
Why did you come back, then?

114
00:10:16,520 --> 00:10:17,810
I came to apologize to you.

115
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:27,580
Can you stay with me?

116
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:31,720
Even if it's just as a friend is fine.

117
00:10:41,810 --> 00:10:42,500
Alright,

118
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:46,290
I'll keep you company.

119
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:49,700
I'll be in my room.

120
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:51,300
Let me know if you need anything.

121
00:12:13,280 --> 00:12:14,300
I have something for you.

122
00:12:16,610 --> 00:12:17,890
Guess what it is.

123
00:12:21,830 --> 00:12:22,840
Flowers?

124
00:12:25,230 --> 00:12:26,730
What's the occasion?

125
00:12:28,670 --> 00:12:29,870
It's not flowers.

126
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:31,950
Want to know what it is?

127
00:12:32,500 --> 00:12:33,190
Mm.

128
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:34,600
Close your eyes.

129
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:37,640
Open your hand.

130
00:12:41,810 --> 00:12:42,810
Now, open your eyes.

131
00:12:45,950 --> 00:12:47,600
I made this scented candle myself.

132
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:49,010
It's tulip-scented.

133
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,080
When you come home tired
after a long day at work,

134
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:54,210
the tulip scent can help.

135
00:13:02,630 --> 00:13:03,920
I feel refreshed.

136
00:13:05,370 --> 00:13:06,400
I told you

137
00:13:06,410 --> 00:13:08,400
the scent would help.

138
00:13:10,610 --> 00:13:12,210
You're the one who helped me.

139
00:13:18,610 --> 00:13:19,400
Chris...

140
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:21,100
Please come back to me soon.

141
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:33,820
Do I have to get rid of her...

142
00:13:35,700 --> 00:13:37,800
for Chris to love me?

143
00:13:57,030 --> 00:13:59,980
You want me to look into this woman

144
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:01,200
for what, exactly?

145
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:02,920
I want to know everything she does

146
00:14:03,290 --> 00:14:04,840
and everyone she knows.

147
00:14:11,210 --> 00:14:14,640
Is there any specific information
you'd like to know?

148
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,480
I don't know either.

149
00:14:17,020 --> 00:14:18,400
But that's exactly why

150
00:14:18,990 --> 00:14:21,990
I need to know everything about her.

151
00:14:23,410 --> 00:14:25,390
Whatever she's planning to do

152
00:14:25,410 --> 00:14:26,690
or how she does it.

153
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:30,910
Seeing your expression

154
00:14:30,990 --> 00:14:32,380
makes me a little worried.

155
00:14:32,710 --> 00:14:35,310
I'm not helping out a villain, right?

156
00:14:37,980 --> 00:14:40,300
You might think I'm a villain,

157
00:14:40,660 --> 00:14:42,610
but what you're doing

158
00:14:43,300 --> 00:14:45,410
will definitely save someone.

159
00:15:12,900 --> 00:15:13,900
Serves you right.

160
00:15:14,210 --> 00:15:15,440
I told you,

161
00:15:15,690 --> 00:15:17,400
if you'd approached her directly

162
00:15:17,710 --> 00:15:19,620
and told her everything outright,

163
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:21,420
things would've been a lot easier.

164
00:15:22,490 --> 00:15:23,270
No,

165
00:15:23,450 --> 00:15:24,990
if I'd approached Chris

166
00:15:25,510 --> 00:15:26,910
and told her the truth outright,

167
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:33,480
this would've happened before
she ever fell in love with me.

168
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:35,400
Ugh!

169
00:15:35,500 --> 00:15:37,400
Can you stop speaking in riddles?

170
00:15:38,160 --> 00:15:40,130
You still haven't told me

171
00:15:40,150 --> 00:15:41,910
what happened to Chris yesterday.

172
00:15:45,570 --> 00:15:46,610
It's hard to explain.

173
00:15:47,700 --> 00:15:49,530
I can hardly believe it myself.

174
00:15:50,590 --> 00:15:52,530
What happened, then?

175
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:54,800
Chris remembered

176
00:15:57,100 --> 00:15:59,920
that I was the other woman in
her relationship with Nadear.

177
00:16:00,210 --> 00:16:00,990
What?!

178
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:04,210
Don't ask me why.

179
00:16:04,890 --> 00:16:06,890
I'm trying to figure that out myself.

180
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:21,610
Hey, Kiiro.

181
00:16:26,020 --> 00:16:26,690
Chris,

182
00:16:26,756 --> 00:16:28,900
I ordered some coffee for you.
Do you want it now?

183
00:16:30,400 --> 00:16:31,420
Nadear...

184
00:16:32,110 --> 00:16:33,600
This isn't Kiiro.

185
00:16:37,830 --> 00:16:39,000
You can tell?

186
00:17:03,930 --> 00:17:07,560
[Aquatic Veterinary Hospital]

187
00:17:10,700 --> 00:17:11,500
Hello?

188
00:17:13,900 --> 00:17:14,900
Then...

189
00:17:19,260 --> 00:17:22,910
do you know where I can
find a similar-looking fish?

190
00:17:26,210 --> 00:17:28,100
It took me so long

191
00:17:28,120 --> 00:17:30,710
to find a fish that looks like Kiiro.

192
00:17:31,910 --> 00:17:34,190
But you could still tell the difference.

193
00:17:34,700 --> 00:17:35,820
I'm a little disappointed...

194
00:17:38,500 --> 00:17:39,810
Why did you do this?

195
00:17:42,110 --> 00:17:43,470
If I hadn't found out,

196
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:45,800
would you still have kept
hiding the truth from me?

197
00:17:47,120 --> 00:17:49,650
I just didn't want you to be sad.

198
00:17:54,190 --> 00:17:55,280
Can you stop trying to protect me

199
00:17:55,290 --> 00:17:57,320
by lying to me like this, Nadear?

200
00:18:00,520 --> 00:18:02,290
I raised Kiiro myself.

201
00:18:03,620 --> 00:18:06,110
If it died, I want to know how.

202
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:09,600
I want to be able to grieve for it, too.

203
00:18:11,410 --> 00:18:12,720
Don't act like it didn't matter

204
00:18:12,730 --> 00:18:14,800
and replace it so easily.

205
00:18:19,490 --> 00:18:21,410
Whether it's a fish or a dog,

206
00:18:22,700 --> 00:18:24,600
there's only one Kiiro for me.

207
00:18:44,390 --> 00:18:47,220
[Third Person]

208
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:51,220
[Third Person]

209
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:08,110
Jeen...

210
00:19:13,600 --> 00:19:15,020
Are you alright?

211
00:19:16,420 --> 00:19:17,780
What's wrong?

212
00:19:18,730 --> 00:19:20,300
I'm just scared.

213
00:19:25,450 --> 00:19:26,540
Is it because of me?

214
00:19:40,170 --> 00:19:41,720
It was my fault.

215
00:19:41,740 --> 00:19:43,210
I betrayed you.

216
00:19:46,330 --> 00:19:47,660
I'm sorry.

217
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:52,250
I won't do it again.

218
00:20:00,720 --> 00:20:01,930
Good...

219
00:20:04,020 --> 00:20:06,220
Then can you tell me

220
00:20:07,630 --> 00:20:10,080
if the memories you've given Chris

221
00:20:11,740 --> 00:20:14,460
will always stay that way?

222
00:20:17,270 --> 00:20:19,310
Nothing else will interfere with

223
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:22,330
her memories again, right?

224
00:20:25,930 --> 00:20:28,010
Chris just knows more now.

225
00:20:30,020 --> 00:20:32,100
She knows you're her girlfriend.

226
00:20:33,820 --> 00:20:36,030
And that Sun is the other woman
in this relationship.

227
00:20:39,260 --> 00:20:42,330
That's how she'll remember things

228
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:48,540
as long as you keep
taking care of her like you used to.

229
00:20:52,730 --> 00:20:53,730
And...

230
00:20:55,020 --> 00:20:56,920
bring her to see me as usual.

231
00:21:00,100 --> 00:21:01,230
Alright.

232
00:21:06,120 --> 00:21:09,250
As long as Chris
doesn't get back with Sun,

233
00:21:10,210 --> 00:21:11,810
I still have hope.

234
00:21:13,930 --> 00:21:14,900
What about me?

235
00:21:17,930 --> 00:21:19,860
I'm living

236
00:21:20,930 --> 00:21:22,740
for you right now, Jeen.

237
00:21:34,650 --> 00:21:36,870
You don't have to do this.

238
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:42,340
You've helped me out,

239
00:21:45,720 --> 00:21:48,020
so let me help you for once.

240
00:21:57,430 --> 00:21:58,430
I know...

241
00:21:59,020 --> 00:22:00,020
you want this.

242
00:22:02,750 --> 00:22:05,030
Can I ask you something?

243
00:22:05,630 --> 00:22:06,520
Hm?

244
00:22:15,130 --> 00:22:17,670
Can you make Chris love me

245
00:22:20,610 --> 00:22:23,700
the way you love me?

246
00:22:32,140 --> 00:22:33,420
That way...

247
00:22:34,930 --> 00:22:36,520
you can love me

248
00:22:37,820 --> 00:22:39,430
however you want.

249
00:22:47,430 --> 00:22:50,080
[Third Person
Bar - Bistro]

250
00:22:58,250 --> 00:22:58,940
Come in.

251
00:22:59,670 --> 00:23:00,840
Chris!

252
00:23:00,860 --> 00:23:02,980
A customer wants to speak to the manager.

253
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:05,820
She said there's something wrong
with the flower in her food.

254
00:23:06,320 --> 00:23:07,940
Chris... Help me, please.

255
00:23:07,970 --> 00:23:09,820
She's so scary.

256
00:23:10,220 --> 00:23:11,520
I'll go check it out.

257
00:23:14,140 --> 00:23:15,140
Um...

258
00:23:15,920 --> 00:23:17,230
She's over there.

259
00:23:22,030 --> 00:23:23,520
Wawah, you can get back to work.

260
00:23:23,820 --> 00:23:24,820
I can take care of this.

261
00:23:26,020 --> 00:23:27,020
Okay.

262
00:23:38,130 --> 00:23:39,930
Could you tell me
what's wrong with the dish?

263
00:23:49,740 --> 00:23:51,830
Well...

264
00:23:53,330 --> 00:23:55,720
I've had better elsewhere.

265
00:24:00,430 --> 00:24:02,420
Then you should go back to that place.

266
00:24:15,210 --> 00:24:16,620
That's why I came here.

267
00:24:19,620 --> 00:24:21,330
You must be mistaken.

268
00:24:22,320 --> 00:24:23,840
You were never here.

269
00:24:24,720 --> 00:24:26,220
But the place I came from...

270
00:24:28,320 --> 00:24:29,420
had you in it.

271
00:24:31,730 --> 00:24:32,730
Sun...

272
00:24:35,950 --> 00:24:38,320
I don't want to make the same mistake.

273
00:24:41,420 --> 00:24:42,420
I know.

274
00:24:44,690 --> 00:24:45,710
And?

275
00:24:48,820 --> 00:24:51,320
Neither do I.

276
00:24:58,680 --> 00:24:59,710
Why are you here?

277
00:25:01,930 --> 00:25:02,930
I miss you.

278
00:25:05,040 --> 00:25:06,040
I want to see you.

279
00:25:33,020 --> 00:25:34,020
That's all.

280
00:25:35,820 --> 00:25:36,820
I'll...

281
00:25:37,320 --> 00:25:38,320
I'll get going now.

282
00:25:40,760 --> 00:25:41,850
Thank you so much.

283
00:25:46,260 --> 00:25:48,210
Take care, alright?

284
00:25:48,410 --> 00:25:52,240
♫Trapped in a love that's a fading image,♫

285
00:25:52,260 --> 00:25:56,020
♫Yet the love that never faded♫

286
00:25:56,040 --> 00:26:02,490
♫Like a missing page I can't find♫

287
00:26:02,510 --> 00:26:05,510
♫Your smell lingers vividly in my mind♫

288
00:26:05,530 --> 00:26:12,230
♫The touch from when you were by my side♫

289
00:26:12,310 --> 00:26:15,800
♫You're still so clear in my heart♫

290
00:26:15,820 --> 00:26:19,380
♫But who are you?♫

291
00:26:19,630 --> 00:26:22,420
♫...Please tell me♫

292
00:26:48,140 --> 00:26:51,140
[Private Investigator]

293
00:26:57,750 --> 00:26:58,640
Alright.

294
00:26:59,220 --> 00:27:00,910
Can we meet today?

295
00:27:07,070 --> 00:27:08,700
Ever since the accident,

296
00:27:09,310 --> 00:27:10,530
Chris and Nadear

297
00:27:10,540 --> 00:27:12,520
haven't posted any photos on social media.

298
00:27:14,230 --> 00:27:16,030
They've left all their group chats.

299
00:27:17,430 --> 00:27:19,420
No one except their parents

300
00:27:19,630 --> 00:27:21,830
can get in touch with them anymore.

301
00:27:23,430 --> 00:27:25,690
It's like they want to
cut ties with their old lives.

302
00:27:31,230 --> 00:27:34,660
The private investigator Chicha
recommended sure is the real deal, huh?

303
00:27:37,080 --> 00:27:38,620
So what are you gonna do next?

304
00:27:45,730 --> 00:27:47,830
No matter what I say,

305
00:27:48,830 --> 00:27:50,410
Chris won't believe me.

306
00:28:14,620 --> 00:28:16,130
I love you, Nadear.

307
00:28:20,430 --> 00:28:22,010
Well done, Jeen.

308
00:28:23,880 --> 00:28:25,760
I felt so satisfied

309
00:28:25,780 --> 00:28:27,420
when I saw Chris turn her back on Sun.

310
00:28:28,920 --> 00:28:31,020
I should've done this a long time ago.

311
00:28:38,920 --> 00:28:39,920
Where are you going?

312
00:28:43,720 --> 00:28:45,300
You already know where.

313
00:28:49,320 --> 00:28:51,330
Be a good girl, alright?

314
00:29:06,600 --> 00:29:07,420
Nadear?

315
00:29:14,640 --> 00:29:15,640
So,

316
00:29:16,230 --> 00:29:17,340
my sister

317
00:29:17,820 --> 00:29:19,530
wants to be a lapdog

318
00:29:20,160 --> 00:29:21,320
instead of a doctor?

319
00:29:23,440 --> 00:29:24,830
Why are you here, Prung?

320
00:29:25,240 --> 00:29:27,170
I came to warn you.

321
00:29:27,570 --> 00:29:29,120
You're the other woman

322
00:29:29,140 --> 00:29:30,510
in this relationship now.

323
00:30:15,310 --> 00:30:17,310
I don't want to make the same mistake.

324
00:30:18,920 --> 00:30:21,120
Neither do I.

325
00:30:22,620 --> 00:30:23,720
Why are you here?

326
00:30:24,620 --> 00:30:25,620
I miss you.

327
00:30:27,210 --> 00:30:28,610
I want to see you.

328
00:30:49,820 --> 00:30:51,430
[Chris]

329
00:30:51,440 --> 00:30:52,700
[Decline Call]

330
00:31:06,620 --> 00:31:09,100
Could my memories be distorted

331
00:31:09,110 --> 00:31:10,800
or incomplete?

332
00:31:15,720 --> 00:31:18,300
I can't believe I cheated

333
00:31:19,120 --> 00:31:22,120
and loved the other woman
as much as I loved Sun.

334
00:31:33,060 --> 00:31:33,990
[Could my memories be distorted

335
00:31:34,000 --> 00:31:34,820
or incomplete?]

336
00:31:34,840 --> 00:31:35,840
[I can't believe I cheated

337
00:31:35,850 --> 00:31:36,830
and loved the other woman
as much as I loved Sun]

338
00:31:43,540 --> 00:31:44,300
Oh?

339
00:31:44,680 --> 00:31:46,100
You're still awake?

340
00:31:47,030 --> 00:31:48,330
Where have you been?

341
00:31:48,520 --> 00:31:50,470
I went to talk to Nan.

342
00:31:51,510 --> 00:31:52,620
Have I told you

343
00:31:52,630 --> 00:31:54,100
I've already fired Nan?

344
00:31:54,120 --> 00:31:55,910
And I'm going to sue her, too.

345
00:31:56,110 --> 00:31:57,420
And she's okay with that?

346
00:31:58,550 --> 00:31:59,580
Of course not.

347
00:32:00,320 --> 00:32:02,520
She even said she'd sue me back.

348
00:32:02,930 --> 00:32:04,110
What a waste of my time.

349
00:32:05,480 --> 00:32:06,720
Thank you, Nadear,

350
00:32:08,230 --> 00:32:10,630
for everything you've done for me

351
00:32:11,100 --> 00:32:12,410
and our restaurant.

352
00:32:14,120 --> 00:32:14,900
From now on,

353
00:32:14,910 --> 00:32:17,340
I'll be the best friend you
could ever ask for.

354
00:32:46,540 --> 00:32:48,420
Can we talk, Nan?

355
00:32:52,120 --> 00:32:54,920
I want to see you one last time,

356
00:32:54,940 --> 00:32:56,510
and I won't bother you again.

357
00:33:06,620 --> 00:33:09,690
[Third Person]

358
00:33:10,653 --> 00:33:13,713
[Third Person]

359
00:33:21,413 --> 00:33:22,123
So?

360
00:33:22,613 --> 00:33:24,783
Hasn't your girlfriend hurt me
enough already?

361
00:33:25,323 --> 00:33:26,403
Nan,

362
00:33:26,713 --> 00:33:29,113
you were the one who stole
from Nadear and me.

363
00:33:29,363 --> 00:33:31,213
So you found out about Sun...

364
00:33:31,463 --> 00:33:32,313
and Nadear,

365
00:33:32,323 --> 00:33:33,553
and you still talk to me like this?

366
00:33:36,133 --> 00:33:37,133
I knew it.

367
00:33:37,923 --> 00:33:40,793
How can an ordinary conversation compare to pillow talk?

368
00:33:43,403 --> 00:33:44,333
Nan,

369
00:33:44,723 --> 00:33:46,703
I called you out here

370
00:33:46,723 --> 00:33:48,033
so we could settle things properly

371
00:33:48,513 --> 00:33:50,553
and you'd finally stop pestering Nadear.

372
00:33:50,913 --> 00:33:51,913
What the hell?

373
00:33:52,433 --> 00:33:54,993
After that slap, I never
did anything to her again.

374
00:33:55,473 --> 00:33:57,523
I sold her my shares

375
00:33:58,213 --> 00:33:59,923
and let her deduct the amount
from what I still owed her.

376
00:34:00,823 --> 00:34:02,723
Nadear said she came
to settle things with you.

377
00:34:02,913 --> 00:34:04,513
And weren't you going to sue her back?

378
00:34:04,533 --> 00:34:05,413
Chris,

379
00:34:05,733 --> 00:34:07,513
don't be so stupid.

380
00:34:08,613 --> 00:34:10,013
Your girlfriend

381
00:34:10,023 --> 00:34:11,333
is one hell of a schemer.

382
00:34:11,593 --> 00:34:13,103
Who's gonna do anything to her?

383
00:34:14,213 --> 00:34:15,043
Oh...

384
00:34:15,613 --> 00:34:18,333
I guess only an idiot like you

385
00:34:18,713 --> 00:34:19,673
would believe her.

386
00:34:22,013 --> 00:34:23,103
What a fucking waste of my time.

387
00:34:24,033 --> 00:34:25,033
Nan,

388
00:34:25,513 --> 00:34:26,883
don't you ever talk about
Nadear like that again.

389
00:34:28,173 --> 00:34:28,793
Let go!

390
00:34:29,533 --> 00:34:30,213
Let me go!

391
00:34:33,813 --> 00:34:35,613
Is this what you want?

392
00:34:37,353 --> 00:34:38,353
Fine.

393
00:34:39,833 --> 00:34:40,833
Nan, I...

394
00:34:44,183 --> 00:34:45,913
You two are both pieces of shit.

395
00:34:48,523 --> 00:34:49,623
Don't bother me again!

396
00:34:59,033 --> 00:35:00,623
I bought this for you.

397
00:35:04,443 --> 00:35:05,123
Wait!

398
00:35:09,813 --> 00:35:10,493
Chris!

399
00:35:17,353 --> 00:35:21,023
[Emergency Room]

400
00:35:24,873 --> 00:35:25,913
Are you alright, Chris?

401
00:35:27,613 --> 00:35:28,623
I'm okay.

402
00:35:29,123 --> 00:35:30,523
Thanks for helping me.

403
00:35:31,613 --> 00:35:32,613
Good thing

404
00:35:32,643 --> 00:35:34,113
I got there early.

405
00:35:35,913 --> 00:35:37,603
What did you want to tell me?

406
00:35:38,313 --> 00:35:39,433
Just say it.

407
00:35:41,213 --> 00:35:43,223
About your memories...

408
00:35:44,513 --> 00:35:45,623
I told you

409
00:35:46,223 --> 00:35:47,613
I remembered everything.

410
00:35:49,623 --> 00:35:50,823
Are you sure?

411
00:35:52,393 --> 00:35:54,423
When you said you remembered everything,

412
00:35:55,623 --> 00:35:57,613
were there really no
unanswered questions left?

413
00:36:02,023 --> 00:36:03,313
What are you trying to say?

414
00:36:06,513 --> 00:36:07,413
Chris.

415
00:36:13,923 --> 00:36:14,813
Sun.

416
00:36:16,483 --> 00:36:17,803
It's nothing, Nadear.

417
00:36:18,023 --> 00:36:19,713
Sun brought me here.

418
00:36:25,713 --> 00:36:26,823
Let's go home, then.

419
00:36:28,023 --> 00:36:30,103
The police have arrested Nan.

420
00:36:30,823 --> 00:36:32,713
Don't do this again, Chris.

421
00:36:33,803 --> 00:36:35,903
Can't I do something for you for a change?

422
00:36:36,913 --> 00:36:38,643
You've already done so much for me.

423
00:36:45,033 --> 00:36:45,793
Miss.

424
00:36:49,513 --> 00:36:51,433
We used to be close in
high school, weren't we?

425
00:36:52,913 --> 00:36:54,213
You know me well,

426
00:36:56,613 --> 00:36:58,303
so don't act like we're strangers.

427
00:37:06,313 --> 00:37:07,593
Nice hair, Nadear.

428
00:37:21,723 --> 00:37:22,723
Chris,

429
00:37:24,223 --> 00:37:25,223
your wound...

430
00:37:29,813 --> 00:37:31,003
I'm fine.

431
00:37:31,113 --> 00:37:32,333
I'll go rest up.

432
00:37:33,723 --> 00:37:35,323
What were you talking about with Sun?

433
00:37:40,813 --> 00:37:41,813
It's nothing.

434
00:37:42,223 --> 00:37:44,133
I just thanked her for helping me.

435
00:37:44,923 --> 00:37:46,713
Then let's go see Dr. Jeen

436
00:37:47,013 --> 00:37:48,673
once you feel better.

437
00:37:49,033 --> 00:37:49,713
Hm?

438
00:37:50,923 --> 00:37:52,813
Maybe you can't love me

439
00:37:53,013 --> 00:37:55,593
because you feel guilty.

440
00:37:56,813 --> 00:37:58,753
I want you to get therapy

441
00:37:59,823 --> 00:38:02,123
so maybe we can fall in love again.

442
00:38:32,393 --> 00:38:33,613
Thanks for coming.

443
00:38:35,803 --> 00:38:37,203
Let's put an end to this

444
00:38:39,913 --> 00:38:41,703
once and for all, okay?

445
00:38:43,413 --> 00:38:44,623
The reason you came here...

446
00:38:45,413 --> 00:38:48,353
is that you still have doubts, right?

447
00:38:49,223 --> 00:38:51,013
Just get to the point.

448
00:38:52,633 --> 00:38:54,633
I don't want to make
the same mistake again.

449
00:38:56,423 --> 00:38:57,813
Neither do I.

450
00:39:02,013 --> 00:39:03,013
Chris...

451
00:39:04,423 --> 00:39:06,313
I lost my memory once.

452
00:39:09,013 --> 00:39:11,523
I thought I could remember
everything again,

453
00:39:15,113 --> 00:39:16,673
but that wasn't the case.

454
00:39:17,933 --> 00:39:19,033
Perhaps

455
00:39:20,613 --> 00:39:22,923
hearing about past events

456
00:39:23,673 --> 00:39:26,013
could give you false memories.

457
00:39:29,443 --> 00:39:30,793
Are you saying

458
00:39:31,413 --> 00:39:33,533
the memories I got back

459
00:39:34,723 --> 00:39:36,103
aren't real?

460
00:39:43,323 --> 00:39:45,023
This isn't funny, Sun.

461
00:39:47,803 --> 00:39:50,813
If you're trying to convince
me to believe something this ridiculous,

462
00:39:52,493 --> 00:39:53,493
please stop.

463
00:40:04,533 --> 00:40:06,123
Do you really believe

464
00:40:07,213 --> 00:40:08,523
our relationship...

465
00:40:10,763 --> 00:40:13,013
was just a fleeting romance

466
00:40:14,213 --> 00:40:16,523
you never wanted in the first place?

467
00:40:18,843 --> 00:40:20,593
Is that really what you believe?

468
00:40:35,093 --> 00:40:37,923
If it was something more than that,

469
00:40:40,213 --> 00:40:43,223
can you trust me one last time?

470
00:40:48,723 --> 00:40:52,303
I want you to remember everything yourself.

471
00:40:58,913 --> 00:41:00,523
Remember everything myself?

472
00:41:04,243 --> 00:41:05,193
How?

473
00:41:07,073 --> 00:41:08,413
Go find Tangdong.

474
00:41:12,683 --> 00:41:13,903
"Tangdong" is the name of someone

475
00:41:13,913 --> 00:41:15,813
who might be able to help you remember.

476
00:41:16,913 --> 00:41:18,113
That's enough, Sun.

477
00:41:20,293 --> 00:41:22,313
I really want to end this.

478
00:41:28,813 --> 00:41:30,013
Do you know why

479
00:41:31,013 --> 00:41:32,933
I didn't take you

480
00:41:32,953 --> 00:41:35,153
to meet Tangdong?

481
00:41:41,213 --> 00:41:42,813
What are you trying to pull this time?

482
00:41:44,023 --> 00:41:46,313
I want to end this, too.

483
00:41:46,973 --> 00:41:49,213
But you have to remember

484
00:41:50,213 --> 00:41:52,803
the truth yourself.

485
00:42:15,633 --> 00:42:16,513
Tangdong?

486
00:42:19,363 --> 00:42:20,513
Who's that?

487
00:42:28,173 --> 00:42:30,353
Who... are you?

488
00:42:34,313 --> 00:42:35,223
Uh...

489
00:42:35,823 --> 00:42:36,923
I...

490
00:42:39,093 --> 00:42:40,843
Just kidding, you dummy.

491
00:42:41,103 --> 00:42:41,753
Oh my God, Chris!

492
00:42:41,773 --> 00:42:43,393
I miss you so much!

493
00:43:06,183 --> 00:43:07,393
What happened?

494
00:43:08,133 --> 00:43:09,133
Where is Chris?

495
00:43:10,103 --> 00:43:11,103
I don't know.

496
00:43:12,383 --> 00:43:15,283
She texted me saying she had
something urgent to take care of.

497
00:43:15,403 --> 00:43:16,533
Don't worry.

498
00:43:17,913 --> 00:43:20,113
She didn't even answer my call.

499
00:43:23,923 --> 00:43:25,513
She'll be back soon.

500
00:43:27,873 --> 00:43:29,093
I'm scared.

501
00:43:30,413 --> 00:43:31,543
You said

502
00:43:31,553 --> 00:43:34,523
you could manipulate Chris' memories

503
00:43:35,113 --> 00:43:37,803
because she lost her memories.

504
00:43:38,233 --> 00:43:40,083
Whatever information we feed her,

505
00:43:40,103 --> 00:43:41,063
her brain

506
00:43:41,073 --> 00:43:43,903
will fill in the gaps to make sense of it.

507
00:43:45,403 --> 00:43:46,353
That's right.

508
00:43:47,323 --> 00:43:49,213
The human brain is complex.

509
00:43:49,713 --> 00:43:51,503
Her amnesia

510
00:43:51,653 --> 00:43:52,833
is like being lost,

511
00:43:53,013 --> 00:43:54,613
with all these doors around her.

512
00:43:55,413 --> 00:43:57,613
And until she finds the door
that leads to the truth,

513
00:43:57,773 --> 00:44:00,003
her brain is ready to imagine things

514
00:44:00,023 --> 00:44:02,813
or create new memories
based on what we feed her.

515
00:44:03,293 --> 00:44:05,313
That's why I tried...

516
00:44:06,913 --> 00:44:08,813
to keep her from seeing anyone.

517
00:44:12,303 --> 00:44:13,133
Nadear,

518
00:44:14,003 --> 00:44:15,523
even if she does meet someone,

519
00:44:17,263 --> 00:44:19,213
she still might not remember.

520
00:44:27,003 --> 00:44:29,583
[Third Person]

521
00:44:30,984 --> 00:44:33,624
[Third Person]

522
00:44:47,164 --> 00:44:47,934
Chris,

523
00:44:52,354 --> 00:44:53,504
you're back?

524
00:45:00,514 --> 00:45:02,124
Where have you been?

525
00:45:03,124 --> 00:45:05,254
I went to see someone named Tangdong.

526
00:45:06,834 --> 00:45:08,104
Do you know her?

527
00:45:10,824 --> 00:45:12,334
A close friend

528
00:45:12,344 --> 00:45:14,044
who knows everything about me,

529
00:45:16,024 --> 00:45:17,214
you,

530
00:45:19,334 --> 00:45:20,314
and Sun.

531
00:45:26,884 --> 00:45:29,224
You lost your memories, too?

532
00:45:29,934 --> 00:45:30,654
Whoa...

533
00:45:30,814 --> 00:45:32,114
This is straight out of a movie.

534
00:45:32,914 --> 00:45:33,654
Here.

535
00:45:38,124 --> 00:45:39,414
Several months ago,

536
00:45:39,624 --> 00:45:41,304
Sun ran into me.

537
00:45:41,614 --> 00:45:43,284
I showed her the photo album,

538
00:45:43,304 --> 00:45:44,304
and that made her remember.

539
00:45:50,934 --> 00:45:52,624
Aren't there any photos of Nadear?

540
00:45:54,614 --> 00:45:55,614
Nadear?

541
00:45:56,714 --> 00:45:58,064
Your best friend?

542
00:45:59,624 --> 00:46:02,194
She was in a different class
in high school,

543
00:46:02,634 --> 00:46:03,904
so there aren't many photos of her.

544
00:46:05,324 --> 00:46:06,554
I didn't take many photos

545
00:46:06,564 --> 00:46:08,474
in middle school.

546
00:46:08,494 --> 00:46:09,204
If I had,

547
00:46:09,214 --> 00:46:11,024
you'd have a lot of
photos with Nadear.

548
00:46:18,214 --> 00:46:19,214
What about Sun?

549
00:46:21,324 --> 00:46:22,504
Sun...

550
00:46:22,524 --> 00:46:24,104
she transferred to our school
in 11th grade.

551
00:46:24,464 --> 00:46:25,614
She was the new kid.

552
00:46:25,974 --> 00:46:28,104
Then she joined our group.

553
00:46:28,414 --> 00:46:30,244
We had so much fun back then.

554
00:46:30,504 --> 00:46:32,214
She was really close to me.

555
00:46:33,374 --> 00:46:34,644
Mm...

556
00:46:34,924 --> 00:46:36,124
But you two didn't start dating

557
00:46:36,134 --> 00:46:38,514
until... your first or
second year of university.

558
00:46:39,124 --> 00:46:40,204
Sun told me

559
00:46:40,214 --> 00:46:41,654
not to tell anyone about
your relationship,

560
00:46:42,034 --> 00:46:43,604
because she didn't want
her family to find out.

561
00:46:43,824 --> 00:46:44,974
And look how that turned out.

562
00:46:45,234 --> 00:46:47,424
You both lost your memories.

563
00:46:47,444 --> 00:46:49,024
Good thing I still remember.

564
00:46:55,344 --> 00:46:56,424
Do you know her?

565
00:46:58,004 --> 00:46:59,004
Tangdong.

566
00:47:01,814 --> 00:47:03,014
Of course.

567
00:47:03,534 --> 00:47:05,814
Tangdong was in our class, too.

568
00:47:07,034 --> 00:47:08,224
No!

569
00:47:10,934 --> 00:47:13,094
Stop lying already, Nadear!

570
00:47:16,514 --> 00:47:17,514
You too, Doc.

571
00:47:18,324 --> 00:47:19,894
What did you do to my memories?

572
00:47:20,914 --> 00:47:21,624
Huh?!

573
00:47:22,414 --> 00:47:23,524
What did you do?!

574
00:47:24,004 --> 00:47:26,214
Chris... calm down.

575
00:47:41,024 --> 00:47:42,614
Did you go to see her again?

576
00:47:44,814 --> 00:47:47,014
She must have messed with
your head again.

577
00:47:49,424 --> 00:47:50,114
No,

578
00:47:51,214 --> 00:47:52,944
I went to see Tangdong myself.

579
00:47:53,874 --> 00:47:55,704
And I told Sun to come here.

580
00:47:58,014 --> 00:48:00,414
Sun used to live here, right?

581
00:48:13,724 --> 00:48:16,414
I can't remember my relationship with Sun

582
00:48:19,424 --> 00:48:21,504
because you and Dr. Jeen

583
00:48:22,734 --> 00:48:24,654
rewrote my memories of Sun,

584
00:48:29,014 --> 00:48:30,804
turning them into memories
of my relationship with you.

585
00:48:41,424 --> 00:48:42,424
Chris...

586
00:48:45,124 --> 00:48:48,324
We were just friends this entire time.

587
00:48:53,704 --> 00:48:55,254
Somchai, why did you pick on my friend?

588
00:48:55,714 --> 00:48:56,304
What?

589
00:48:56,314 --> 00:48:57,374
I didn't do anything.

590
00:48:57,524 --> 00:48:59,214
She just cried for no reason.

591
00:48:59,234 --> 00:49:00,454
What's that in your hand, then?

592
00:49:00,484 --> 00:49:02,394
You won't even let me
have a bite, you meanie!

593
00:49:02,724 --> 00:49:03,784
Take it back, then!

594
00:49:03,804 --> 00:49:05,774
You already bit a chunk out of it!

595
00:49:05,804 --> 00:49:07,544
Stop picking on my friend!

596
00:49:08,424 --> 00:49:09,534
Ugh!

597
00:49:12,624 --> 00:49:14,404
It's alright, I'll buy you
a new one.

598
00:49:16,314 --> 00:49:17,494
Here, take this.

599
00:49:34,624 --> 00:49:37,284
Did you know Aom and Nam from my class

600
00:49:37,514 --> 00:49:38,614
are dating now?

601
00:49:40,114 --> 00:49:41,214
How would I know?

602
00:49:41,234 --> 00:49:42,914
I'm not even in your class.

603
00:49:44,294 --> 00:49:45,724
But isn't Aom into guys?

604
00:49:48,914 --> 00:49:50,514
Probably not anymore.

605
00:49:51,624 --> 00:49:53,964
So... how do you feel about

606
00:49:53,974 --> 00:49:55,484
Aom dating a girl?

607
00:49:57,834 --> 00:49:58,934
I'm fine with it.

608
00:49:58,954 --> 00:50:00,004
It's kinda sweet.

609
00:50:01,514 --> 00:50:03,524
So, if a girl flirted with you,

610
00:50:03,544 --> 00:50:04,964
would you be okay with that?

611
00:50:06,734 --> 00:50:08,324
What are you talking about?

612
00:50:08,344 --> 00:50:09,604
I wouldn't want that.

613
00:50:09,634 --> 00:50:11,174
I'm not even into girls.

614
00:50:34,314 --> 00:50:34,924
Here.

615
00:50:36,224 --> 00:50:37,714
Did you buy these to give to people?

616
00:50:38,374 --> 00:50:39,014
No,

617
00:50:39,034 --> 00:50:40,104
they're offerings to the Buddha.

618
00:50:41,314 --> 00:50:43,314
Then no thanks. I don't want to
take one meant for Buddha.

619
00:50:45,614 --> 00:50:47,324
This one isn't an offering.

620
00:50:47,924 --> 00:50:49,524
I bought this for you.

621
00:51:00,484 --> 00:51:01,224
Wait!

622
00:51:01,304 --> 00:51:02,014
Chris!

623
00:51:06,204 --> 00:51:06,814
Huh?

624
00:51:17,034 --> 00:51:18,504
I've always thought of you

625
00:51:19,784 --> 00:51:22,204
as one of my closest friends.

626
00:51:24,474 --> 00:51:25,324
No,

627
00:51:30,514 --> 00:51:33,114
I was never your friend.

628
00:51:37,774 --> 00:51:38,724
I...

629
00:51:42,324 --> 00:51:44,414
I've always loved you.

630
00:51:46,344 --> 00:51:48,724
Is this how you treat someone you love?!

631
00:51:50,714 --> 00:51:53,524
You changed your hairstyle
and hair color to look like Sun.

632
00:51:55,014 --> 00:51:57,624
You stole my memories with Sun.

633
00:52:03,524 --> 00:52:04,974
You hypnotized me...

634
00:52:07,614 --> 00:52:09,914
into remembering you instead of Sun.

635
00:52:14,224 --> 00:52:15,314
In the end,

636
00:52:17,174 --> 00:52:18,834
I'm the one who's broken!

637
00:52:18,854 --> 00:52:21,204
You broke me!!

638
00:52:27,234 --> 00:52:28,504
And you know what?

639
00:52:29,814 --> 00:52:31,814
I really hated myself.

640
00:52:33,224 --> 00:52:34,454
I hated myself for loving you

641
00:52:34,464 --> 00:52:36,804
and holding you dear in my memories.

642
00:52:39,414 --> 00:52:41,734
But when I'm with you...

643
00:52:42,474 --> 00:52:46,124
I feel terrible every time we touch!

644
00:52:49,304 --> 00:52:51,084
I could only think of

645
00:52:51,114 --> 00:52:54,704
and yearn for whatever the hell
I'd never be able to find!

646
00:53:00,034 --> 00:53:01,024
Did you know?

647
00:53:01,804 --> 00:53:04,334
You didn't just take away
the woman I loved.

648
00:53:07,014 --> 00:53:10,494
You took away my closest friend, too!

649
00:53:10,904 --> 00:53:12,604
How could you be so cruel, Nadear?!

650
00:53:12,624 --> 00:53:14,654
How could you do this to me?

651
00:53:15,644 --> 00:53:16,504
Chris!

652
00:53:17,924 --> 00:53:20,214
I took away the woman you love?

653
00:53:21,914 --> 00:53:24,174
She was the one who left you!

654
00:53:27,624 --> 00:53:30,934
When you were on the brink of death
and lost your memories,

655
00:53:33,114 --> 00:53:35,974
the woman you loved
was the one who left you!

656
00:53:38,474 --> 00:53:41,414
I was the one who always
stayed by your side.

657
00:53:43,814 --> 00:53:46,324
But you kept thinking only about her!

658
00:53:46,344 --> 00:53:48,304
What else was I supposed to do?!

659
00:53:52,554 --> 00:53:53,964
Tell her, Sun!

660
00:53:55,024 --> 00:53:57,884
Tell her you were
the one who left Chris first!

661
00:54:11,184 --> 00:54:12,194
Is this

662
00:54:14,604 --> 00:54:16,894
what you've been trying
to apologize to me for?

663
00:54:24,824 --> 00:54:25,824
Yes...

664
00:54:36,714 --> 00:54:38,704
I'm... I'm sorry, Chris.

665
00:54:39,224 --> 00:54:40,114
Chris...

666
00:54:43,724 --> 00:54:45,114
I'm sorry...

667
00:55:03,524 --> 00:55:04,294
Sun.

668
00:55:04,934 --> 00:55:05,824
Sun...

669
00:55:07,334 --> 00:55:08,104
Sun.

670
00:55:10,434 --> 00:55:11,824
Are you alright, Sun?

671
00:55:19,084 --> 00:55:20,224
What's wrong?

672
00:55:21,614 --> 00:55:22,574
I love you...

673
00:55:22,594 --> 00:55:24,114
I'm sorry...

674
00:55:24,134 --> 00:55:25,374
Sun... look at me, Sun.

675
00:55:25,394 --> 00:55:26,604
Sun. Sun. Look at me.

676
00:55:26,624 --> 00:55:28,474
- Sun, look at me.
- Hey!

677
00:55:28,514 --> 00:55:29,684
- Focus on me.
- Nadear!

678
00:55:29,704 --> 00:55:30,594
Nadear!

679
00:55:30,614 --> 00:55:31,134
Nadear!

680
00:55:31,544 --> 00:55:32,854
- Nadear!
- Let go!

681
00:55:32,914 --> 00:55:33,914
Let go of me!

682
00:55:34,774 --> 00:55:37,304
I will never let you take
Chris away from me again!

683
00:55:39,124 --> 00:55:40,124
- Nadear, don't!
- Nadear!

684
00:55:40,144 --> 00:55:40,694
Nadear.

685
00:55:40,714 --> 00:55:41,764
- Stop!
- Nadear!

686
00:55:41,784 --> 00:55:43,414
- Nadear!
- Put away the gun, Nadear!

687
00:55:43,434 --> 00:55:44,104
Nadear!

688
00:55:46,614 --> 00:55:47,504
Chris!

689
00:55:52,514 --> 00:55:53,544
Nadear!

690
00:55:54,234 --> 00:55:54,984
Let go!

691
00:56:00,224 --> 00:56:01,524
Sun... Sun.

692
00:56:01,544 --> 00:56:03,024
Doc... take care of Sun first.

693
00:56:03,634 --> 00:56:04,964
Sun... Sun.

694
00:56:05,394 --> 00:56:06,104
Sun. Sun!

695
00:56:06,124 --> 00:56:06,824
Sun...

696
00:56:06,834 --> 00:56:07,634
Sun!

697
00:56:12,324 --> 00:56:13,204
Chris!

698
00:56:13,844 --> 00:56:15,224
I'm sorry!

699
00:56:19,614 --> 00:56:20,534
Chris!

700
00:56:22,834 --> 00:56:25,714
Chris is not yours anymore, Nadear.

701
00:56:25,934 --> 00:56:28,294
The tumor near my brainstem is back.

702
00:56:29,014 --> 00:56:30,924
I might forget everything about you again.

703
00:56:31,614 --> 00:56:33,124
I slept with Jeen

704
00:56:33,294 --> 00:56:35,134
in exchange for

705
00:56:35,154 --> 00:56:37,534
tampering with your memories.

706
00:56:37,734 --> 00:56:40,724
If the surgery works this time...

707
00:56:41,034 --> 00:56:42,254
What if I lose my memories again?

708
00:56:42,924 --> 00:56:44,104
It's okay.

709
00:56:44,914 --> 00:56:45,974
Just come back.

710
00:56:46,524 --> 00:56:47,654
I don't want to forget.

711
00:57:01,264 --> 00:57:10,594
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

712
00:57:11,144 --> 00:57:16,274
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

713
00:57:16,304 --> 00:57:19,914
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

714
00:57:20,604 --> 00:57:26,334
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

715
00:57:26,354 --> 00:57:35,804
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

716
00:57:36,184 --> 00:57:41,234
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

717
00:57:41,254 --> 00:57:45,534
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

718
00:57:45,554 --> 00:57:54,474
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

719
00:57:54,914 --> 00:58:03,074
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫
